WEBVTT

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:10.900
To fight against messengers from the future who are changing history to erase soccer...

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.530
...we, the Raimon Eleven, are now traveling through time to assemble the strongest eleven in history.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.790
Dear Heavenly Father, please protect France.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.360
That's...

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.880
It's a real war.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.780
Yeah.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.490
Armor and shields and swords!

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:21.250
It's a virtual game in real life!

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.670
Just how much defensive power have they got?

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.930
Who cares about that right now?

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.620
This is bad! This is really bad!

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.630
How do we find Jeanne d'Arc in this situation?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.550
She should be in a town called Vaucouleurs...

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:39.490
Who's there?!

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.220
What do we do...

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.300
How do we explain ourselves?

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.770
We got lost while we were running away from the fighting.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.650
We wish to go to Vaucouleurs.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.310
What?

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.820
You don't belong in this country, do you!

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:02.870
W-Well...

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.770
Who are these people?

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.360
They're foreigners.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.720
They say they are lost, but I think they're rather suspicious.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:16.460
Suspicious?

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:17.830
Yes, sir.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.530
They say they want to go to Vaucouleurs.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.370
What? Don't tell me you're after Jeanne!

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.970
Um, I'm not sure about that.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:27.850
Jeanne!

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:29.850
That's her?

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.770
You're Jeanne d'Arc?

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.380
How do you know my name?

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.550
She's different from what I imagined.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.600
Yeah...

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.530
She's wearing glasses.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.790
She doesn't look anything like an authoritative fighting maiden.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.520
Hiya! I'm Kinako!

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.120
Nice to meet you!

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.480
What are you doing?!

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.830
That's going a bit overboard...

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.040
Jeanne, I bet they're spies from England!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:57.710
Spies?

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.050
No! No, we're not!

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.770
We've come from the future!

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.050
We want you to help us.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.260
The... future?

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.060
What do you mean, the future?

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:11.850
Well...

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.870
What is she doing?

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.900
It looks like she can't see through her glasses clearly.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.500
Um... please answer me.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.240
Why turn to Kirino?

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.830
She's mistaking who she's asking.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.050
Well...

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.000
What we mean is...

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:46.750
We should be honest and tell her about time traveling.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.800
I don't think she'd understand.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.040
Yeah.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:54.410
This is a time period where anything strange was thought to be the work of the devil.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.810
Yeah, it could end badly.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.160
No way...

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.710
Well? Say something!

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.630
You <i>must</i>  be spies!

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:06.780
In that case, we cannot allow you to live!

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:09.950
Please wait!

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:11.240
Why are you stopping us?

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.340
Well... um...

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:15.500
I know!

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.070
It's candy.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.270
Please take it.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:28.140
Take it?

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.020
Have a taste.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.230
Right now?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.410
Yes, right now.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:43.820
It's good!

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.990
Thank goodness!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.320
Would you like some too?

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:53.790
Here you go.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.790
It's so good!

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.790
Why don't the rest of you have some, too?

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.750
T-Thanks!

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.600
How is it?

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:03.880
Is it really that good?

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.130
It really is that good!

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.090
It has such a naturally gentle flavor.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.810
Here Tsurugi, for you.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.500
How is it?

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.060
It's good.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.980
She's just a normal girl.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.450
She's cute.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.820
Jeanne!

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.530
What are you doing?

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:33.240
Um...

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.080
I'm showing consideration.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.320
I don't think that's quite right.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:41.080
Interacting with others in this way so that I can get to know them better is important.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.420
You're right!

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.630
Yeah, it's really important!

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:48.270
Never mind that, hurry up and decide what we should do with them!

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.020
Um, well...

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.100
At any rate, we can't just leave them here.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:58.520
Let's take them with us to Vaucouleurs.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:16.450
Next.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:17.580
Sir!

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.140
How about it? Did you feel that awesome power in you?

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:43.750
You did, right?

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.020
Yes, Zanark-sama.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:49.730
Then you can snuff out those Raimon small fries easily, right?

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.240
Smart!

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.950
Now that we have Zanark-sama's power, there is no reason for us to lose.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:58.410
I thought you'd say that.

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.300
Well, things took a weird turn.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.760
Yeah.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.260
You don't think we're going to get enlisted into this war, do you?

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:22.370
Or we may even be executed as spies of the enemy!

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.690
Hey, hey, anything but that.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.400
And we only just met Jeanne d'Arc...

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:30.360
We'll have to watch the situation for now.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.640
We'll find a chance to Mixi-max with her one way or another.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.410
But will we really get stronger Mixi-maxing with that Jeanne-san?

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.270
She does have a point.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.870
Yeah, I don't feel any power from that girl at all.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:49.590
In any case...

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.300
Why don't we practice?

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:54.630
Practice?

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:55.780
Yeah!

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.740
I'm sure things will work out.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.300
For now, let's just chase the ball.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.270
Things will work out, huh?

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.730
Okay then, let's do it!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.270
What?

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.230
What are they doing?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.980
One against one, and imagine that you're in front of the goal!

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.820
Shinsuke, are you ready?

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.150
Yep!

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.660
Want to go against me?

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:22.120
Sounds interesting.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:27.830
Here I go!

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.630
Not bad.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:42.890
You can defend too.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.230
I can do a lot of positions.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.190
Oh, you're really skillful, Nanobana-san.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.690
Why are you so formal all of a sudden?

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.360
Just call me Kinako like you always do.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.030
I-Is that right?

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.490
Like I always do.

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:05.450
I didn't expect a new time paradox to occur.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.730
What do you think caused it?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:08.950
I don't know.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:12.170
But we can't mess up the flow of time anymore than we already have.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.380
Yeah.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:18.840
We need to get stronger, strong enough so that we won't lose no matter who comes after us.

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.350
Tenma, want to think up a hissatsu technique for the two of us?

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.470
I've been wanting to do one with you for some time now.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:28.770
That sounds like a great idea!

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:31.260
Tenma!

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:32.190
Okay!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.070
What is that you are doing?

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.190
Miss Jeanne!

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:45.990
It's soccer!

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:48.080
Soccer?

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:49.490
Yes!

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:52.080
It's the most important thing to us.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.310
The most important thing?

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:55.170
Yes.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:58.050
We came here because we want to protect soccer.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.740
For that, we traveled through time-

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:02.840
Tenma!

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:06.720
I don't think you will understand if we explained to you now.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.180
But we need your help.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.690
Is soccer really that precious to you?

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.180
Yes.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:18.070
It's an extremely fun sport that gets us excited.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:20.390
I know!

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.410
Have you ever seen this?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.830
We can even do this!

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.460
Wow.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:40.090
Soccer seems so interesting.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:50.120
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.010
Kirino!

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:13.370
Um, please take these.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.040
Thanks! You start wanting something sweet after you exercise!

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.180
You're so thoughtful!

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:20.450
I like you!

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:23.630
Um, I just wanted to learn more about you people.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:28.330
Miss Jeanne, you said giving out candy was an act of consideration, right?

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:29.890
I think that's a lovely thought.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:31.730
Really?

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:35.690
I get the feeling that we're going to be great friends, don't you?

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.050
Friends...

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.110
Why, yes!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:42.900
Now!

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:46.070
Huh?

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:49.900
Stop!

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:52.640
What if someone saw you?!

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.140
They'll definitely think that we're hostile!

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.110
I couldn't take her aura.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:02.300
She's different from the Jeanne that we know.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:05.330
Her power hasn't awakened yet.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:08.370
So it's the opposite from Nobunaga?

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:09.760
That's how it is, I suppose.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.710
So, do you like soccer?

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.490
Um...

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.900
It looks interesting, but I still don't understand it.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:26.430
To put it simply...

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.740
Soccer is like war.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.660
W-War?

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.080
Yep!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.300
You move to keep the ball from getting stolen.

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:39.380
From there, everyone works together to defend and attack.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.050
Everyone works together...

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.630
How do you get everyone to work together?

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:51.150
Well, there are various ways to do it...

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.100
But I guess the first step is exchanging passes.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:54.530
"Passes"?

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.040
Want to try it?

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.350
O-Okay!

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:03.410
Let's try it again!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:07.150
Oh no!

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:09.680
No, no, it's okay!

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:11.870
You did it!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.080
I did it...

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:13.830
I did it!

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:17.350
This next one is going to be a little stronger!

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:24.240
You're with me this time.{Kirino... you've been guillotined!}

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:25.170
I find that reassuring.

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.010
I see...

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.020
I'm sorry!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:35.940
Here.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:37.520
T-Thank you.

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:39.980
How is it? Are you having fun?

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.600
It's fun.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:47.160
Somehow, I can feel the other person's emotions through the ball.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:51.820
Maybe the ball connects all of our hearts together by an invisible thread.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.810
So this is soccer.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.210
You don't have to stand guard over them anymore.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.920
Please let them move freely.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:06.880
Are you certain?

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:08.350
Yes.

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:11.970
I don't think they are spies.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.680
Why is that? How can you be so sure?

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:19.730
While we were on our way back here, I saw a strange light in the sky.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.190
And then these people showed up.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:30.190
They may be the helping hand we need that God has sent to us.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.200
These people?

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:39.130
If that is God's will, then it is destiny that they come with me.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:49.480
How beautiful.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:50.670
Jeanne.

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.320
I can't lie after all.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.810
That light you saw was indeed us.

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.600
But it has nothing to do with God's will.

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.400
Oh no...

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:03.810
Then how did you come about here?

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.590
I'm sorry, I can't say.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:09.150
But our desire to protect soccer is true.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.570
That's why we're here.

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:16.530
If you help us, we can protect what's precious to us.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:21.500
Are you saying I have that sort of power?

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:24.460
With you, we can do it.

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:32.270
I have that sort of power?

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:35.430
I don't even know if I can fend off the English army.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.030
Jeanne.

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:44.650
Does the battle scare you?

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.440
Then why are you guiding these men?

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:52.440
Because God told me to.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:54.400
God told you?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:17:00.450
God told me to protect Orléans and save France.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.250
Did He really tell you that?

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:04.940
Yes!

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:06.550
He did!

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:09.620
God assigned me to be a guide.

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:12.670
So I have to do it!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.940
You don't believe me, do you.

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:22.830
I doubt anybody does.

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:26.690
But it's true. I really did hear Him.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.280
I wasn't hearing things.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:36.620
No matter how scared I am, I have to keep moving forward.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:37.810
Jeanne...

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:44.870
Coming!

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:47.620
Miss Jeanne!

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:53.590
Um, I need to go see King Charles tomorrow and ask him for reinforcements.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:55.050
Reinforcements?

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:56.650
Yes.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:18:01.250
We need them to free the city of Orléans that is under the siege of the English army.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:03.660
So, um...

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:06.870
Can you come with me, as an escort?

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:08.810
An escort?

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:16.100
From what you've told me, your soccer tactics may be useful for crossing enemy lines.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:19.210
Crossing enemy lines?

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.620
That's dangerous!

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:25.830
Once we bring back reinforcements and free Orléans safely,

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:29.370
I will do everything in my power to help you.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.590
Okay.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.920
We need Jeanne's power.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:45.260
So if Jeanne needs our power, we should help her.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:47.480
Kirino-senpai...

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:49.390
You're right.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:51.940
Thank you, everyone!

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.540
Then let's all go!

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.590
We get to wear armor, right?

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:59.070
Yeah, yeah! I want to try wearing that!

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.070
I wonder what kind of weapons there are.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.260
Um...

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:08.000
The carriage can only hold seven people, so only six of you will be able to come with me.

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:10.460
Then...

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.940
The more of you who come, the more reassuring it would be for me, but...

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.230
I'm sorry.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:23.370
Then put this here...

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:25.140
It's so hard to move in.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:27.350
I can't see in front of me!

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.930
That's the wrong size for you.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.440
Wah, this is heavy!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.480
I don't know how you manage to wave that thing around.

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:39.760
Well... the truth is, I can't use it very well either.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.450
Really?

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:46.940
But if the time calls for it, I must brandish the sword.

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:48.330
No matter how scared I am.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.830
Please, let me go.

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:57.190
I'm begging you.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.240
Okay.

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.380
Take care of the others.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:10.740
You're coming along too, I see.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:11.810
Um...

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.660
My name?

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:14.980
It's Kirino Ranmaru.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:16.930
Ranmaru...

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:18.480
It's good to be with you.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:20.350
Yeah.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:29.380
Guys, we're all going to protect Jeanne.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:32.590
Stay focused, just like how we are during our games.

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:33.330
Okay!

00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:37.230
Will Jeanne-san's power really awaken?

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:39.250
It will.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:42.040
We'll get the Mixi-max to work no matter what!

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:46.940
Someone who rouses up the team's courage, changing it into an iron-wall defense...

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:48.620
I wonder how that's like!

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.730
Um, good morning.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:56.690
Let's go!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:58.570
Okay!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:15.410
I hope King Charles sends out reinforcements.

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:17.910
He must...

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.420
It's God's will.

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.600
Our new enemy, Zanark.

00:22:55.600 --> 00:23:01.350
This nameless member of the lower middle class who leads Protocol Omega comes barging into the middle of a war!

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:03.820
Next, Soccer Within The Flames!

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.480
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:19.540
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:21.930 --> 00:23:26.330
Interacting with others so that I can get to know them better is important.

00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:27.370
That's all!
